course: dictionary
lesson: 1666
title: The chloroplast
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A chloroplast is a tiny green part inside a plant cell. Its job is photosynthesis: it uses sunlight to make food, a sugar, from water and carbon dioxide.
explain: While it works, a chloroplast gives off oxygen, which is the air we breathe. Chloroplasts are found in plant cells, not in animal cells. Look for the word «chloroplasts» in the sentence: the clues are «in green parts» and «catch light», so they are the parts that catch sunlight.
explain: The green colour comes from chlorophyll, the green pigment inside chloroplasts. That is why leaves look green. When you label a cell diagram, you write chloroplast next to the nucleus, cell wall and vacuole.
fact: A chloroplast is a tiny green part inside plant cells.
fact: Photosynthesis happens in chloroplasts: they use sunlight to make sugar from water and carbon dioxide.
fact: Photosynthesis gives off oxygen.
fact: Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll, the green pigment that makes leaves green.
fact: Animal cells do not have chloroplasts.
exercise: «Plant cells have a stiff wall, a nucleus and, in green parts, chloroplasts that catch light.» Where would you find chloroplasts? | In the cell wall of the stem | In the nucleus | In animal cells | *In green parts of plant cells
exercise: What does a chloroplast use sunlight to make? | Stiff walls | *Sugar, a food for the plant | Dark dots | Chlorophyll
exercise: Which gas does photosynthesis in a chloroplast give off? | Sunlight | Iodine | *Oxygen | Carbon dioxide
test: What green pigment is found inside chloroplasts? | Vacuole | Iodine | Nucleus | *Chlorophyll
test: Do animal cells have chloroplasts? | Yes, in the nucleus | Yes, in every cell | Only in the dark | *No, only plant cells have them
exam: Where are chloroplasts found, and what do they do? | In the cell wall, where they stop leaks | Inside animal cells, where they make muscles | *Inside green plant cells, where they make sugar using sunlight | In the nucleus, where they store water
